<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<worksheet  xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Fuel Efficiency of a Marine Motor</title>

  <objectives>
          <ul>
                  <li>
                        The Learner will investigate how derivatives of functions affect the
                        derivative of new functions obtained by combining them.
                  </li>
          </ul>
  </objectives>
  <introduction>
        <p>
                The fuel consumption (in gallons per hour) and power output (in horsepower) of
                some marine (boat) motors are available in their technical specifications as
                functions of the running speed of the motor (in revolutions per minute).
        </p>
        <p>
                For the boat motor we are looking at, we will call the \emph{fuel Consumption
function} <m>C</m>, and we will call the <em>Power output fuction</em> <m>P</m>.
        </p>
        <p>
                You work at a marine engine company, and your job today is to determine the <em>Volumetric Fuel Efficiency</em> (<m>VFE</m>) of an engine and determine how the efficiency changes with engine speed.  The Volumetric Fuel Efficiency is the amount of work (in horsepower-hours) that can be done for a specific amount of fuel (so the final units will be horsepower-hours per gallon).
        </p>
        <p>
Here is the information you have:
                <ul>
                <li> <m>C(1800)=17.61</m></li>
                <li> <m>P(1800)=61.09</m></li>
                <li> <m>C'(1800)=0.01776</m></li>
                <li> <m>P'(1800)=0.07141</m></li>
                </ul>
        </p>
  </introduction>
  <exercise workspace="1in">
          <introduction>
                  <p>
                        Here is an outline of your job for this activity:
                  </p>
          </introduction>
        <task>
                <statement>
                        <p>
                                Interpret each of the values listed above in the context of this
                                task;
                        </p>
                </statement>
        </task>
        <task>
                <statement>
                        <p>
                                Determine the relationship among <m>C</m>, <m>P</m>, and <m>VFE</m>. 
                        </p>
                </statement>
        </task>
        <task>
                <statement>
                        <p>
                                Calculate <m>VFE(1800)</m>.
                        </p>
                </statement>
        </task>
        <task>
                <statement>
                        <p>
                                Estimate <m>VFE'(1800)</m> and interpret the results.
                        </p>
                </statement>
        </task>
  </exercise>
</worksheet>
